    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nRayconor is superbly private and is accessed through impressive gates and a tree-lined avenue. The property oozes character and style and has been the secluded guest house for many celebrities over the past decade.\n\nThe residence, set on 10 Acres and situated in Gurtymadden, Loughrea, was originally built in the 1850s and remained in the same ownership until its current owner acquired it in 2006. \n\nIts owner, has sensitively renovated and remodelled and indeed extended this home to retain its old-world charm while providing all modern conveniences. \n\nRayconor is one of those rare opportunities to acquire a private estate in this stunning countryside. Viewing is highly recommended and is STRICTLY by appointment."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall/ Boot Room - 2.89m x 3.33m\nAccess to this properties wonderful accommodation is via Narnia-style double doors to its stone finish entrance lobby, wooden floor\n\nSitting/Entertainment Room - 4.46m x 3.42m\nWonderful sitting room/entertainment room, dual aspect windows, feature solid fuel fireplace, wooden floor\n\nOpen Plan Kitchen/Living Room - 4.52m x 8.94m\nDual aspect windows, base units, feature solid fuel fireplace, wooden flooring\n\nGuest wc - 1.76m x 0.92m\nSide access window, whb/wc, wooden floor\n\nSnug/Office - 1.82m x 2.66\nFront aspect window, feature stone wall, wooden flooring\n\nKitchen/Living - 6.68m x 3.83m\nQuirky kitchen with its own charming solid fuel fireplace, the kitchen also leads to the aforementioned patio via glass double doors. A seperate staircase facilitates access to a gorgeous bedroom/den overhead with Ensuite.\n\nBedroom/Den - 1.82m x 2.66m\nAccess from kitchen staircase, rear aspect windows, wooden flooringEnsuite: 0.86m x 3.96mwhb/wc/shower, tiled floor\n\nFirst Floor Level - \n\n\nBedroom 1 (Master) - 6.69m x 3.46m\nDual aspect windows, feature solid fuel fireplace, wooden floorA full bathroom suite is found off the master, whb/wc/roll top bath, shower, wooden flooring\n\nBedroom 2 (Dressing Room) - 3.54m x 2.12m\nCurrently used as the the owner's full dressing room, rear aspect window, wooden floor\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.56m x 2.59m\nRear aspect window, wooden floor\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.50m x 4.02m\nSide aspect window, feature stone wall, wooden floorEnsuite: 0.95m x 3.12mRear aspect window, whb/wc/shower, tiled floor\n\nBathroom - 1.99m x 2.05m\nRear aspect window, whb/wc/roll top bath with overhead shower, wooden floor\n\nGrounds - \nThe properties grounds comprise a double stone car port, six box stables and yard, tack room, outdoor storage shed, four bay hayshed, small sand arena, and extensive mature gardens.\n\n"
      },
